<title>GERMANY: Metro up after confirms 1996 forecast.</title>
<headline>Metro up after confirms 1996 forecast.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German retailer Metro AG were higher in pre-bourse IBIS electronic dealings after the retailer said 1996 group sales were unchanged at 62 billion marks and it expected at least one billion marks in profit.</p>
<p>The profit forecast was the same as earlier predicted by Metro, which was created last year by the merger of retailer Kaufhof and Asko Deutsche Kaufhaus by Swiss-based parent Metro.</p>
<p>Metro shares were up 1.30 marks at 126 marks after earlier reaching 127.80 marks, outpacing the 30-share DAX index which was up 18.90 points at 3,086.38, or up 0.62 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
